  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At Port Santa Lucia in Saint-Raphaël, Le Pescadou serves traditional Mediterranean cuisine made with fresh, local produce — fresh seafood, generous portions praised in reviews — in a warm décor extended by a terrace overlooking the harbour. Two consistent platforms give it an excellent rating: 4.8/5 (280+ reviews) and 4.9/5 on Restaurant Guru (848 reviews). Pets are tolerated, information not re-sourced independently during our latest check but not contradicted either.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>This is a pleasant address for a meal facing the boats, with a menu that showcases local produce. As with many harbourside addresses, the terrace tables are the most sought after.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: ask directly for a terrace table on arrival, that's where the Port Santa Lucia atmosphere is best enjoyed with your dog at your feet.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Port Santa Lucia and its quays are perfect for a digestive walk after the meal.</p>
